    "text": "Role: Composer, conductor, arranger\nAffiliation: Hall Johnson Choir (founder, 1925); Festival of Negro Music & Drama\nBio: Concert spiritual arranger whose dialect settings were controversial and foundational. The Hall Johnson Choir established the all-Black professional concert choir as a viable form.\nTags: black-sacred, composer-arranger, professional, historical",
