    "id": "conductors/william-levi-dawson",
    "page": "conductors",
    "pageTitle": "Conductors Directory",
    "title": "William Levi Dawson",
    "text": "Role: Composer, conductor\nAffiliation: Tuskegee Institute (Director of the School of Music, 1931–1956)\nBio: Built the Tuskegee Choir into a national institution. His Negro Folk Symphony (1934) and spirituals arrangements (Ezekiel Saw de Wheel, Soon-Ah Will Be Done) remain programming staples.\nTags: black-sacred, composer-arranger, collegiate, hbcu, historical",
    "url": "https://kevinphillipjohnson.com/academy/conductors.html"
